From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: howeasy <howardabudd@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:45:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] slink: Polished Crystal trainers, starters, statics, trades

PolishedCrystalRomHandler reads and writes trainer parties, the Elm's Lab
starters, the resolved givepoke/loadwildmon statics and gifts, and the NPC
trades. Every writer rewrites only a site's two species bytes in place,
keeping the site's gender and form bits; formed mons are never in the model,
INVER's WRAM pool is never walked, and a trainer record whose walk does not
end at its size prefix refuses. A changed party size, level, item, move list,
or trade nickname/OT/DV/item throws instead of being written. EGG, the unused
$100, Unown and the variant forms leave the pools. Rival and Lyra triples are
tagged so "rival carries starter" works. A second INI section (CopyFrom)
admits the SLink companion overlay (header checksum 0x725C).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
