+## Patch 18 — Polished Crystal trainers, starters, statics/gifts, NPC trades
+- `PolishedCrystalRomHandler`: readers and writers for trainers, starters, statics/gifts and NPC trades. Every
+  writer rewrites only a site's two species bytes in place (LOW, HIGH<<5 with the site's gender and form bits
+  kept); only NO_FORM/PLAIN_FORM sites are in the model, so formed mons are never read or written. Variant
+  forms fold to their species; EGG, the unused $100 and Unown are refused. `setPokemonPool` drops those (and
+  the variant forms) from the main pools; `bannedForStaticPokemon` / `getBannedFormesForTrainerPokemon` ban them.
+- Trainers: TrainerGroups -> per-class size-prefixed records (`db size`, name@, flags, mons with the flag-selected
+  item/DV/personality/nickname@/EV/moves fields); a walk that does not end at the size prefix refuses. INVER's entry
+  points at WRAM and is never walked; records with no plain mon are left out. A changed party size, double
+  battles, or a changed level/item/move list throws (resetMoves is not honoured: the party keeps its moves).
+  Tags: leaders GYM1-16, Elite Four ELITE1-4, CHAMPION, rival RIVAL1-7 and Lyra FRIEND1-5 triples with
+  `forceStarterPosition` on the last mon, so "rival carries starter" works.
+- Starters: the three Elm's Lab givepoke species (pokepic/cry/name text are not rewritten). Statics/gifts: the
+  resolved givepoke/loadwildmon sites outside Elm's Lab; their level byte changes only under a level setting.
+  NPC trades: both species of each 33-byte record; Jeeves (Galarian Weezing) stays out whole; nickname, DVs,
+  item and OT must come back unchanged. `canChangeStaticPokemon` is on. Every other writer still throws.
+- `config/polished_offsets.ini` supplement: `TrainerClassCounts`, `TrainerClassCount`, `InverTrainerClass`,
+  `TradeCount`, `TradeLength`, `StarterSites`, `StaticSite0..43` (validated at load: a site must be a PLAIN_FORM
+  givepoke/loadwildmon species), and a `[Polished Crystal SLink overlay (U) 3.2.3]` section for the SLink companion
+  overlay (header checksum 0x725C) via the new `CopyFrom=` key.
